      <!-- Content -->
      <section style="margin: 10rem 30rem">
        <p style="margin-left: 13rem">
          partners, or residents live in the same facility and consent to the
          arrangement.” In addition, Health and Safety Code 1569.269(a)(17): “To
          reasonable accommodation of resident preferences concerning room and
          roommate choices.” Facility will make every attempt to provide a
          compatible roommate but cannot accommodate all residents with
          roommates. In this case a private room may be more suitable.
        </p>
        <ol start="5" style="font-size: 12rem; margin-left: 13rem">
          <li>Food Services:</li>
          <ol type="a" style="margin-left: 25rem">
            <li>Three nutritious daily meals and snacks.</li>
            <li>Special diet, if prescribed by a physician.</li>
          </ol>
          <li>Helping gain access to supportive services which may include:</li>
          <ol type="a" style="margin-left: 25rem">
            <li>Arrange medical and dental appointment</li>
            <li>Other health care services</li>
            <li>Transportation</li>
            <li>Leisure Activités</li>
            <li>Social and Counseling Services</li>
          </ol>
          <li>
            Mom & Dad’s House will assist in making appointments and
            arrangements for transportation for the resident’s medical and
            dental needs.
          </li>
          <ol type="a" style="margin-left: 25rem">
            <li>
              Transportation: Mom & Dad’s House encourages the responsible
              person to transport the resident to medical and dental
              appointments.
            </li>
            <li>
              If the responsible person is unavailable and resident is capable
              of transferring to and from a car with minimal assistance or they
              are pre-registered with Access Transportation services or any
              other wheel chair specialized transportation, with previous
              authorization, Mom & Dad’s House may coordinate transportation and
              provide provide a private companion for the resident under the
              following parameters:
            </li>
            <ol type="i" style="margin-left: 25rem">
              <li>
                Medical or Dental appointments is within an 8 mile radius.
              </li>
              <li>A $______/hour fee will be charged.</li>
              <li>A minimum of 4 hours is required.</li>
              <li>
                Actual cost of transportation will be added. Example cost for
                Uber or Access Transportation.
              </li>
              <li>
                If resident is not capable of making their own decisions,
                responsible party should be available via phone call to provide
                medical information and make medical decisions on behalf of the
                resident.
              </li>
              <li>
                Private Companion will not make any medical decisions on behalf
                of the resident.
              </li>
              <li>
                All transportation arrangements require a minimum of 48 hours
                notice and subject to transportation and caregiver availability.
              </li>
            </ol>
            <li>
              In an urgent situation, medical transport will be called
              immediately. Resident or their insurance are responsible for the
              emergency medical transport charge and will be billed directly by
              the medical transport company.
            </li>
            <li>
              Assistance with personal activities of daily living as follows:
            </li>
            <ol type="a" style="margin-left: 25rem">
              <li>Dressing</li>
              <li>Eating (Including feeding assistance)</li>
              <li>Toileting</li>
              <li>Bathing</li>
            </ol>
          </ol>
        </ol>
      </section>

