      <!-- Content -->
      <section style="margin: 10rem 30rem">
        <ol type="a" start="5" style="font-size: 12rem; margin-left: 60rem">
          <li>Grooming</li>
          <li style="margin-left: -3rem">&nbsp;Mobility Tasks</li>
          <li>
            Other Personal Care Needs: Housework, meals, laundry, taking
            medication, appropriate transportation, correspondence, telephone,
            and related tasks.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <ol start="8" style="font-size: 12rem; margin-left: 20rem">
          <li>
            Basic hygiene items of general use such as soap and toilet paper,
            toothpaste, Kleenex, shampoo, etc. will be furnished, unless the
            resident wants to use or requires a specific brand that the facility
            does not normally purchase. Any item that is for personal use only,
            such as tooth brush, deodorant, razors, shaving items, etc. will be
            provided by each resident or responsible person.
          </li>
          <li>
            Laundering of personal clothing. General laundry service (washing
            and drying of personal laundry. Excluding dry cleaning and ironing.
          </li>
          <li>Clean bed and bath linens weekly, or as often as needed.</li>
          <li>Cleaning of resident’s room.</li>
          <li>
            Comfortable and suitable bed and bedroom furniture. The resident may
            provide his/her own furniture as long as the room will accommodate
            the items. Furniture should be of good quality and safe. Mom & Dad’s
            House reserves the right to reject furnishings if facility believes
            the furniture is not safe or in a state of repair. Mom & Dad’s House
            recommends to bring a NEW mattress for the use of the resident (If
            mattress and linens are brought by the resident or responsible
            party, they shall be brand new and unused, due to risk of
            infestation of bedbugs, scabies, etc. Facility regrets this
            requirement but believes the protection of its residents and staff
            is the highest priority for care and liability.
          </li>
          <li>
            Assistance with taking prescribed and over the counter medication,
            in accordance with physician’s instructions unless prohibited by law
            or regulation, as allowed by Community Care Licensing.
          </li>
          <li>
            Bedside care and tray service for minor temporary illness or
            recovery from surgery. Tray service during the temporary illness or
            recovery surgery is provided without charge for two days. After two
            days, a fee of $______ per day will apply.
          </li>
          <li>
            Coordination and supervision of physical and occupational therapy
            through any necessary outside agencies.
          </li>
          <li>
            Mom & Dad’s House provides access to facility phone for the purposes
            of making local phone calls and receiving phone calls. If resident
            lacks the mental and/or physical capacity to dial phone, facility
            will provide assistance.
          </li>
          <li>
            Coordination of private telephone and cable TV hook-up and service
            (at resident’s expense).
          </li>
          <li>
            To practice universal precautions, facility staff will use gloves
            when caring for all residents.
          </li>
          <li>
            Arrangement optional filed trips, for an extra fee, for the
            utilization of available community resources as follows:
          </li>
        </ol>
        <ol type="a" style="margin-left: 60rem">
          <li>Libraries</li>
          <li>Community Centers</li>
          <li>Senior Centers</li>
        </ol>
        <p style="margin-top: 10rem">
          Subsequent resident appraisals may result in the need for additional
          basic services.
        </p>
      </section>

