      <!-- Content -->
      <section style="margin: 10rem 30rem">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          <b>15. RATE FOR BASIC SERVICES AND PAYMENT PROVISIONS</b>
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          The monthly rate for basic services is $_____ per month.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 6rem">
          Resident or authorized representative understands that the stated
          monthly amount, on a daily pro-rated basis, is due and payable from
          the Date of Admission, not the Move In Date. In the event that the
          designated room is not ready for occupancy on this date, the pro-rated
          amount begins on the date the designated room is ready for occupancy.
        </p>
        <ol style="margin-left: 20rem">
          <li>
            Statements are sent 5 - 10 days before the 1st of the month, which
            will include the rate for basic services and a list of itemized
            optional services incurred by the resident. The monthly fee must be
            paid in advance beginning on the first of the month and due the
            first of every month thereafter.
          </li>
          <li>
            If the basic monthly fee is not received within five days of the due
            date, a late fee of $_______ per day will be assessed for each day
            that the fee is not received.
          </li>
          <li>
            If the fee is not received within 15 days of its due date, eviction
            procedures will begin.
          </li>
          <li>
            Should the facility receive a returned check from the bank, there
            will be a $_____ charge to cover bank fees and special handling
            costs, plus $_____ per day until secured payment is obtained.
          </li>
          <li>
            If the resident is away from the facility for hospitalization,
            vacation, temporary placement outside this facility, etc., the
            monthly rate continues. Individuals other than the resident must
            have the legal right to discharge as determined by the facility upon
            seeing legal documentation. Please note, 30 day notice is required
            to vacate the facility.
          </li>
          <li>
            All financial transactions pertaining to basic and optional services
            will be documented on the resident’s individual file. A copy of the
            file will be provided upon request from the resident or resident’s
            representative.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p style="margin: 12rem 0">The monthly cost is as follows:</p>
        <ol style="margin-left: 60rem">
          <li>
            Basic Service
            Rate:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
            $
          </li>
          <li>
            Cost of optional services
            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;$
          </li>
          <li>
            Hospice Fee
            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;$
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p style="margin-left: 120rem">
          <b
            >TOTAL
            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;$</b
          >
        </p>
        <p style="margin: 8rem 0">Method of payment accepted:</p>
        <ol style="margin-left: 30rem">
          <li>
            Preferred method: ACH Payment, directly through emailed invoice
          </li>
          <li>
            Check. Should Mom & Dad''s House receive a returned check from the
            bank, there will be a $_____ charge to cover bank fees and special
            handling costs.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p style="margin-left: 30rem; margin-top: 8rem">
          Payment should be mailed to:
        </p>
        <p style="margin-left: 30rem">
          Mom & Dad’s House <br />
          12340 Seal Beach Blvd. <br />
          Suite B, Box # 401 <br />
          Seal Beach, CA 90740
        </p>
      </section>

