      <!-- Content -->
      <section style="margin: 30rem">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem"><b>23. PRIVATE COMPANION</b></p>
        <ol style="font-size: 12rem; margin-left: 16rem">
          <li>
            Mom & Dad’s House - does not provide one on one care during the day
            or night. Situations arise when resident needs may <u>require</u> a
            private companion. If a resident requires constant direct
            supervision, Mom & Dad’s House can provide a private companion at an
            additional hourly fee ($_____/hour, if provided by the facility) ,
            until condition has improved. Subject on staff availability.
          </li>
          <li>
            Personal Care Attendants from outside agencies may be used if
            approved by the Administrator. The agency shall ensure a criminal
            clearance on all staff, health screening, appropriate insurance
            including liability and worker’s compensation, proof of appropriate
            employer tax obligations, including but not limited to withholding
            of state and federal taxes, payment of disability and unemployment
            insurance. All appropriate labor laws are to be followed and the
            Personal Care Attendant supervised by an agency administrator
            familiar with facility’s community operations. Agency should provide
            proof to all legal requirements upon request. Any fees incurred in
            obtaining the latter must be paid by resident or resident’s
            representative.
          </li>
          <li>
            All Personal Care Attendants from outside agencies are to be fully
            trained in all legally required topics to be able to assist
            residents in an RCFE environment, prior to coming to Mom & Dad’s
            House to serve a resident. Facility does not provide this training.
          </li>
          <li>Proof of training should be provided upon request.</li>
          <li>
            Personal Care Attendants may not perform any act not allowed by
            regulation or law.
          </li>
          <li>
            The Personal Care Attendant, if employed by an agency, is expected
            to notify his/her supervisor and community staff of any change in
            resident status.
          </li>
          <li>
            The Personal Care Attendants, if employed by an agency, are not to
            provide care at any time to any other resident in the community.
          </li>
          <li>
            It is the responsibility of the agency to ensure proper training of
            the Personal Care Attendant employed by the agency in emergency
            procedures such as fire evacuation, disaster preparedness, etc.
          </li>
          <li>
            Resident or responsible person assumes full responsibility for the
            actions of a private companion.
          </li>
          <li>
            The hiring of a private companion does not alleviate any additional
            levels of care fees as facility must provide all basic and optional
            services and must meet all resident service needs.
          </li>
          <li>
            Resident or resident’s representative is liable for any theft and
            loss that may be caused by the private companion.
          </li>
          <li>
            Any private companion found soliciting other residents for business,
            found to be on the premises without authorization, which
            “substitutes” for other private companions, will be barred from
            entering the property. A private companion is for resident only, and
            not allowed to switch to be a companion for any other facility
            resident.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

