      <!-- Content -->
      <section style="margin: 10rem 30rem">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          <b>24. HOUSE RULES / FACILITY POLICIES:</b>
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          This Admission Agreement provides the resident and responsible person
          with a detailed list of house rules provided at the time of admission.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          The following rules must be observed. Failure to comply, will be
          grounds for eviction.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem"></p>
        <ol style="margin-left: 15rem">
          <li>
            Verbal or Physical abuse directed toward other residents or staff
          </li>
          <li>
            Smoking in the facility is strictly forbidden due to the health and
            safety risks to other residents and to facility staff.
          </li>
          <li>Use of profanity or offensive language</li>
          <li>Purposeful destruction of facility property</li>
          <li>Violent behavior</li>
          <li>Harming or a threat to harm oneself or others</li>
          <li>
            Health conditions, which require staffing level which, are not
            available in the facility
          </li>
          <li>
            Family/visitors which are abusive or upset the general resident
            population
          </li>
          <li>
            Refusal to practice general hygiene techniques such as frequent
            bathing, oral care, clean clothing etc.
          </li>
          <li>
            Refusal to store prescribed and over-the-counter medication,
            nutritional supplements, cleaning products and disinfectants in a
            secured and locked central location to prevent medication errors or
            accidental wrong usage. Resident has a right to privacy and facility
            respects that right. However, having medications in resident room
            without a physician’s authorization may result in facility citations
            and fines by the Department.
          </li>
          <li>
            Noncompliance with physician orders that would result in a threat to
            the safety or wellbeing of the general resident population, i.e.
            refusal to treat an infection.
          </li>
          <li>
            No medication, vitamins or food shall be brought into Mom & Dad''s
            House without staff knowledge
          </li>
          <li>
            Report of any change in health status which would affect the other
            residents or staff
          </li>
          <li>
            Resident theft of facility or other resident belongings. If resident
            family or visitors are witnessed stealing facility or other resident
            belongings, the resident will be held liable for any replacement
            expenses.
          </li>
          <li>
            Possessing or threatening to use a firearm, sharp object or other
            items that may constitute a danger to staff and other residents.
          </li>
          <li>
            Having alcohol or other intoxicating substances without the express
            permission of licensee.
          </li>
          <li>
            In shared rooms, the resident must turn off any audible devices,
            including the television, cell phone, tabloid devices, etc. to
            prevent disturbing other residents. In private rooms, any auditory
            device must be maintained at a sound level that will not disturb
            other residents.
          </li>
          <li>
            The facility may admit individuals whose gender identity or sexual
            orientation differs from most of the resident population. The
            facility does not tolerate discrimination by residents against other
            residents as this may violate the State’s protected civil rights
            that include sex, race, color, religion, national origin, marital
            status, registered domestic partner status, ancestry, actual or
            perceived sexual orientation, or actual or perceived gender
            identity.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

