      <!-- Content -->
      <section style="margin: 30rem">
        <ol start="19" style="margin-left: 20rem">
          <li>
            Resident’s bed, at resident option, may be pushed up against a wall
            in the room if the resident has a clear path and ability to get out
            of bed without obstruction.
          </li>
          <li>
            Facility asks its residents and residents’ visitors to avoid overt
            displays of affection in public and common areas of the facility.
            Facility requests any sexual activities take place in residents’
            rooms only. Residents in shared rooms must be respectful of a
            roommate if and when engaging in consensual sexual activities.
            Facility will attempt to assist with privacy in shared rooms if
            roommates are not consenting to sexual relations with each other.
          </li>
          <li>
            Family members must notify in advance when they are going to take a
            resident out. We need to know what day and the approximate time you
            will be picking the resident up and how long they will be gone so we
            can prepare their medications.
          </li>
          <li>Sign in / Sign Out</li>
          <ol type="a" style="margin-left: 20rem">
            <li>
              Residents are asked to check out when leaving Mom & Dad''s House.
              The person accompanying the resident should do QR code screening
              prior to taking resident out. Residents may not be required to
              disclose their destination. However, for safety purposes the
              resident’s destination may be recorded if it is voluntarily
              disclosed.
            </li>
            <li>
              Residents leaving for extended periods should notify the
              administrator in advance.
            </li>
            <li>
              If residents are out during meal time, it is requested that staff
              be notified that the resident will be out.
            </li>
            <li>
              Upon returning to Mom & Dad''s House, resident or staff may sign
              them in.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </ol>
        <p style="margin: 12rem 0">
          When a resident is first placed in the facility it is particularly
          important that they be giving time to adjust without interference, let
          them know the day(s) and time you will be coming to visit.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          The facility hereby believes these house rules/general policies are
          reasonable and necessary. The resident has the right under California
          State Health and Safety Code 1569.885 to suggest changes to these
          policies.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          <b>25. PROCEDURE FOR SUGGESTING HOUSE RULE CHANGES</b>
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          Facility rules may be changed upon suggestions from the resident. AlI
          resident suggestions must be in writing and presented to the
          Administrator. The Administrator will review written suggestions
          within five working days of receipt. In considering policy changes
          Administrator will present suggested changes to the resident council
          (if one has been established) to ensure no resident right is violated
          or resident safety is compromised if a change occurs. After the review
          of written suggestions, Administrator will render a decision in
          writing to the person who submitted the suggestion.
        </p>
      </section>

