      <!-- Content -->
      <section style="margin: 10rem 30rem">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem"><b>26. FACILITY VISITING POLICY:</b></p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          Mom & Dad''s House encourages regular visits from family, friends and
          clergy.
        </p>
        <ol style="margin-left: 20rem">
          <li>
            Visiting hours at Mom & Dad’s House are from 10:00 AM to 7:00 PM
            every day including holidays.
          </li>
          <li>
            Should you require other visiting times, please contact the
            administrator for advance arrangements
          </li>
          <li>
            All visitors are required to sign in via QR code on a smartphone and
            complete a COVID screening questionnaire prior to entering the
            facility. If the visitor does not have a smart phone device,
            facility staff can provide a smart tablet to complete sign in.
          </li>
          <li>
            After the COVID questionnaire is complete a green or red color
            screen will appear indicating completion. This is to be shown to the
            caregiver on duty where they will allow or deny entry.
          </li>
          <li>Visitors are not allowed in shared rooms.</li>
          <li>
            Mom & Dad’s House requests visitors and families to respect the
            rights of other residents and not to interfere with any patterns of
            resident’s established activities.
          </li>
          <li>
            Visitors are asked to be dressed appropriately and to not smoke in
            facility. Facility prohibits visitors from bringing in cigarettes or
            cigars, lighters, matches, guns, knives or other sharp objects,<u
              ><b> medications</b></u
            >, or money that have not been approved by the administrator.
          </li>
          <li>
            Visitors are welcome to have meals with the resident as long as they
            notify caregivers at least 1 hour before the meal of their intention
            to stay for breakfast, lunch or dinner.
          </li>
          <li>
            Residents can be reached on the phone from 8:00 AM to 7:00 PM. Phone
            calls can be made to Mom & Dad''s House’s number (562) 354-6977, in
            which case the cordless phone is taken to the resident.
          </li>
          <li>
            Mom & Dad’s House will periodically provide resident and resident’s
            representative with notices of facility activities and events. The
            resident’s representative is encouraged to participate.
          </li>
          <li>
            We suggest that all mail is sent directly to the responsible party’s
            address, to avoid delay in getting any important documents.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p style="margin: 12rem 0">
          Mom & Dad’s House - Assisted living facility will ensure that all
          communications to the facility from family and responsible persons
          answered promptly and appropriately. We will encourage regular family
          involvement with the resident and shall provide ample opportunities
          for family participation at the facility. Visitors, including
          ombudspersons and advocacy representatives, are permitted to visit
          privately during reasonable hours and without prior notice, provided
          that the rights of other residents are not infringed upon.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          Resident shall have reasonable access to telephones, to both make and
          receive confidential calls. The facility does require reimbursement
          for long distance calls. Resident will also be able to mail and
          receive unopened correspondence in a prompt manner.
        </p>
      </section>

