      <!-- Content -->
      <section style="margin: 10rem 30rem">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem"><b>61. SURVEILLANCE CAMERAS</b></p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          Facility does not consent to or allow the resident or resident’s
          representative’s use of hidden or exposed cameras or video equipment,
          including the concealed or revealed use of recording equipment in
          resident room or other areas of the facility. It is strictly
          prohibited under California and Federal privacy laws.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 12rem">
          However, facility may use cameras under the following guidance by
          Department of Social Services:
        </p>
        <ol style="margin-left: 20rem">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">
            Mom & Dad’s House - Cottage common areas are monitored by
            surveillance cameras
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">
            Surveillance cameras are for the only purpose of supporting the
            supervision of staff.
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">
            Surveillance cameras do <u>not</u> have an audio component.
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">
            Recordings of the videos taken by the surveillance cameras will not
            be maintained in the residents’ records.
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">
            Surveillance records are stored on an external hard drive that can
            only be accessed by the administrator.
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">
            Surveillance Records will be stored for a limited time and then
            automatically deleted from the system.
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">
            Access to life videos and records require login information and
            password. Only the administrator and managing owners will have
            access to this information.
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">
            Upon request, those with legal authority, will be allowed to view
            any saved recordings.
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">
            Video monitoring equipment and data will be inaccessible to
            unauthorized persons including staff.
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 10rem">Personal Rights:</li>
          <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 1.2em">
            <li style="position: relative; padding-left: 15px">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: 0">-</span>
              <i>Right to privacy in accommodations:</i> Mom & Dad’s House will
              NOT install any cameras in private areas of the residence to
              protect the privacy of our residents.
            </li>
            <li style="position: relative; padding-left: 15px">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: 0">-</span>
              <i>Right to confidentiality of resident records:</i> Surveillance
              records will not be maintained under the residents records. Only
              the administrator, managing owners, and those authorized by law
              will have access to records.
            </li>
            <li style="position: relative; padding-left: 15px">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: 0">-</span>
              <i>Right to have private visits:</i> Surveillance will NOT have an
              audio component to protect residents privacy in their visits and
              conversations.
            </li>
            <li style="position: relative; padding-left: 15px">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: 0">-</span>
              <i>Right to privacy when receiving medical treatment:</i>
              Surveillance cameras will not be installed in any private areas to
              allow our residents to receive privacy when receiving medical
              treatments.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </ol>
        <div
          style="
            margin: 40rem 0 10rem 0;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: flex-end;
          "
        >
          <hr style="width: 240rem; height: 1rem; background-color: #3f3f46" />
          <span style="width: 240rem"
            >Resident or Resident’s Representative</span
          >
        </div>
      </section>

